\begin{takeaways}
\item Archive, compression, authenticity and recoverability are different questions.
\item Inspect the inventory, and practice extraction only with a trusted archive in a new destination.
\item Verify the delivered bytes and rehearse restoring the contents.
\end{takeaways}

\begin{exercise}{Pack just the rota}
\label{ex:23-rota}
Use a new archive named \texttt{rota-only.tar}. The listing
should contain exactly one member, \texttt{handover/rota.txt}.
Leave it for the final cleanup.
\end{exercise}
\begin{solution}
\begin{terminal}
tar -cf rota-only.tar handover/rota.txt
tar -tf rota-only.tar
\end{terminal}
There is no directory operand, so the note is not included.
\end{solution}

\begin{exercise}{Fingerprint a different representation}
\label{ex:23-representation}
Calculate SHA-256 for \texttt{handover.tar} and
\texttt{handover.tar.gz}. Expect different digests even though
decompression restored the tar's bytes. No output file is needed.
\end{exercise}
\begin{solution}
\begin{terminal}
sha256sum handover.tar handover.tar.gz
\end{terminal}
Use the equivalent digest command from the table where required.
\end{solution}

\begin{exercise}{Read the restored note}
\label{ex:23-note}
Using a path under \texttt{recovered}, print the handover note
and compare it with its source. Expect the key desk instruction
and a silent comparison. No additional cleanup is needed.
\end{exercise}
\begin{solution}
\begin{terminal}
cat recovered/handover/key-note.txt
cmp handover/key-note.txt recovered/handover/key-note.txt
\end{terminal}
\end{solution}

\paragraph{Cleanup.}
Check \cmd|pwd -L| against \cmd|"$practice"| first. Only in this
disposable \texttt{utp23} directory, remove the named files,
decline unexpected prompts, then remove the empty directories.
An absent optional exercise file produces a harmless diagnostic.

\begin{terminal}
rm -i ./handover/rota.txt ./handover/key-note.txt
rm -i ./recovered/handover/rota.txt ./recovered/handover/key-note.txt
rm -i ./handover.tar ./handover.tar.gz ./restored.tar ./copy.tar.gz
rm -i ./rota-only.tar
rmdir recovered/handover recovered handover
cd /tmp
rmdir "$practice"
\end{terminal}

Inspect any unexpected leftovers without switching to forced
removal. If you started a separate \cmd|sh|, type \cmd|exit|.
